package mop;

import java.io.*;

/**
 * Regression guard for the log-and-skip rule (INV-ANA-40).
 *
 * The owner `Charset+` is a JDK class, but no import of THIS spec registers
 * `java.nio.charset` — so none of the visitor's three resolution steps answers for it, and
 * it must be logged and skipped. Being a JDK class is not what makes an owner resolvable;
 * the spec importing its package is. That is the same shape as the defect repaired in
 * `generic_new/CharSequence_NotInSet.mop`, which declared `Set+` while importing only
 * java.io/java.lang/java.nio.
 *
 * The owner used to be `Object+`, chosen for the same reason. Phase 5.6 invalidated that
 * choice: the implicit `java.lang` package is now the third resolution step, so `Object`
 * resolves and the fixture stopped witnessing anything. `Charset` is picked because its
 * package is neither imported here nor implicit anywhere — the seed is one package, not a
 * classpath search.
 *
 * This fixture lives under src/test/resources and is deliberately NOT part of any real
 * corpus.
 *
 * @severity error
 */

Unimported_CharsetOwner() {
	event bad_decode before(Object o):
		call(* Charset+.decode(..)) && target(o) {
   android.util.Log.v("RVSEC", __LOC + " ::: Unimported_CharsetOwner");
		}
}
